※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 7000 LANG_COMPTIME_CANNOT

※ The compiler works out what it can before the program runs, and says what it
※ cannot: here a lambda, which nothing yet evaluates while compiling.  The
※ refusal names the construct, so what is missing is something to act on.

let std := ⎕import("std")

fn sizes() → ⸨u8⸩:
    let twice := λ x: u8 → u8 { x + x }
    ⸨twice(3u8)⸩

let known: ⸨u8⸩ = sizes() in ⎕static

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    if known⸨6u8⸩: 0u6 else: 1u6
